It breaks down with skies.

01:33:19.850 --> 01:33:22.930
Tonight was history, and what are we gonna do about it?

01:33:22.930 --> 01:33:23.930
I'm gonna do nothing about it.

01:33:23.930 --> 01:33:26.650
Tonight scared the hell out of me.

01:33:26.650 --> 01:33:28.830
That tank just blew up.

01:33:28.830 --> 01:33:30.000
Whatever happened inside that tank,

01:33:30.000 --> 01:33:32.930
at least a hell of a lot of energy.

01:33:32.930 --> 01:33:35.740
- For God's sake, let's drop this goddamn thing.

01:33:35.740 --> 01:33:36.840
I don't want to talk about it.

01:33:36.840 --> 01:33:38.240
- I can't help it.

01:33:38.240 --> 01:33:39.780
You may want to go to sleep right now,

01:33:39.780 --> 01:33:42.700
but the way I feel, I don't expect to go to sleep for a year.

01:33:42.700 --> 01:33:45.280
I'm on fucking fire.

01:33:45.280 --> 01:33:47.400
I am in there mopping up the goddamn tank room

01:33:47.400 --> 01:33:49.700
and I would like to know why.

01:33:49.700 --> 01:33:51.870
- Do you believe in supernatural agencies, Mason?

01:33:51.870 --> 01:33:53.830
- No, sir, I do not.

01:33:53.830 --> 01:33:57.120
- That what we saw tonight was a physical phenomenon,

01:33:57.120 --> 01:34:00.000
an inexplicable physical phenomenon.

01:34:00.280 --> 01:34:02.800
It's phenomenological and it's explicable, I've got to know why.

01:34:02.800 --> 01:34:06.480
Let me talk, for Christ's sake, I haven't in there mopping up that god damn tank room

01:34:06.480 --> 01:34:11.120
for the last three hours to tell you what I would like to do.

01:34:11.120 --> 01:34:13.670
We have got to repeat this with other human subjects.

01:34:13.670 --> 01:34:15.210
We need a selective sample.

01:34:15.210 --> 01:34:18.350
We will put up a notice in the student union for volunteers, something like that.

01:34:18.350 --> 01:34:20.670
Oh, God almighty, it's Arthur Rosenberg talking, right?

01:34:20.670 --> 01:34:24.320
Go back to square one with them and step up the doses of the drug in a graduated fashion

01:34:24.320 --> 01:34:26.320
and shake them against steady values.

01:34:26.320 --> 01:34:30.000
Oh, I bet you've been even got a grant for Christ's sake!

01:34:32.520 --> 01:34:34.280
and here you are,

01:34:34.340 --> 01:34:36.060
and you use an untested drug

01:34:36.060 --> 01:34:37.820
and it is a human being!

01:34:38.540 --> 01:34:51.630
How are you? Would you like to go back to sleep?

01:34:53.510 --> 01:34:54.860
Yes.

01:34:56.950 --> 01:34:58.750
Would you mind if Mason had a quick look at you first?

01:35:01.880 --> 01:35:06.470
- Good idea.

01:35:06.470 --> 01:35:08.070
- Maybe you oughta have a quick look at it, Mason.

01:36:12.640 --> 01:36:13.640
I hope it isn't the kids.

01:36:13.640 --> 01:36:21.190
Everything's fine, Arthur.

01:36:21.190 --> 01:36:22.190
He's fine.

01:36:22.190 --> 01:36:23.780
It's Arthur.

01:36:23.780 --> 01:36:25.110
Are you fine?

01:36:25.110 --> 01:36:27.470
Yes.

01:36:27.470 --> 01:36:28.470
Arthur, I'll call you back when I'm awake.

01:36:28.470 --> 01:36:29.470
Everything's fine.

01:36:35.210 --> 01:36:36.590
God, I wonder what time it is.

01:36:38.470 --> 01:36:39.540
I should call the kids.

01:36:40.460 --> 01:36:43.610
I can't tell you how much you mean to me.

01:36:44.730 --> 01:36:46.090
How much I need you and the kids.

01:36:46.210 --> 01:36:47.430
I just wanted you to know that.

01:36:48.250 --> 01:36:49.110
You saved me.

01:36:49.210 --> 01:36:50.510
You redeemed me from the pit.

01:36:50.550 --> 01:36:51.330
I was in it, Emily.

01:36:52.010 --> 01:36:56.320
I was in that ultimate moment of terror that is the beginning of life.

01:36:57.300 --> 01:36:57.940
It is nothing.

01:37:00.830 --> 01:37:04.060
hideous, nothing. The final

01:37:04.060 --> 01:37:06.060
truth of all things is that there is

01:37:06.060 --> 01:37:09.550
no final truth. Truth is

01:37:09.550 --> 01:37:11.710
what's transitory. It's human life

01:37:11.710 --> 01:37:13.610
that is real. I don't want to frighten you,

01:37:13.690 --> 01:37:15.530
Emily, but what I'm trying to tell you is that that

01:37:15.530 --> 01:37:17.430
moment of terror is a real

01:37:17.430 --> 01:37:19.490
and living horror, living and growing within

01:37:19.490 --> 01:37:22.930
me now. The only thing that keeps it from devouring

01:37:22.930 --> 01:37:25.660
me is you. Why don't you just come back

01:37:25.660 --> 01:37:30.000
to us? It's too late.

01:37:30.760 --> 01:37:32.820
I don't think I can get out of it anymore.

01:37:32.820 --> 01:37:35.990
I can't live with it. The pain is too great.

01:37:43.410 --> 01:37:46.070
Defy it, Eddie.

01:37:46.070 --> 01:37:48.660
You made it real. You can make it unreal.

01:37:48.660 --> 01:37:51.800
You love me. You love me.

01:37:51.800 --> 01:37:54.200
Eddie, get fired!

01:39:40.650 --> 01:39:41.400
Don't be wrong, boy.

01:42:05.760 --> 01:42:06.240
Thank you.
